==============================================================================
PART A -- the fork 4x4 Dirac matrix and the multiplier solve
==============================================================================
  [PASS] fork Dirac matrix antisymmetric
  [PASS] Pfaffian = L_N K - E c_M  (E enters!)  -- Pf = -E*c_M + K*L_N
  [PASS] det = (L_N K - E c_M)^2
  => still second-class/invertible on the generic branch (L_N K != E c_M);
     the exact-flat-vacuum branch (L_N -> 0 AND c_M -> 0) degenerates as in the
     baseline Gate 6 -- same measure-zero caveat, NOT worse.
  mu_1 (fork) = (E*r_3 + K*r_4)/(E*c_M - K*L_N)
  mu_2 (fork) = (-L_N*r_3 - c_M*r_4)/(E*c_M - K*L_N)
  [PASS] mu_1 = -(K r_4 + E r_3)/(L_N K - E c_M): r_3 now feeds mu_1 through E
  [PASS] E -> 0 recovers certified Gate-8 formula mu_1 = -r_4/L_N
  [PASS] E -> 0 recovers Gate-8 mu_2 = (r_3 - c_M mu_1)/K
  Matter-force channel: mu_1 C_M is the ONLY multiplier term containing matter
  variables (rho_m in C_M); mu_2 S2' and mu_3 S3 are matter-free.  So the matter
  force is set by mu_1 alone, sourced by r_4 AND (new) by r_3 via E.
  NOTE (interior only): {S3, C_M} also carries a rho_m-proportional piece from
  the gamma-dependence of rho_m (density weight); it corrects the mu_1 equation
  by a rho*mu_1 term INSIDE matter and vanishes identically in vacuum. All
  magnitudes below are evaluated on vacuum exteriors, where it is exactly absent.

==============================================================================
PART B -- r_4 and r_3 on the fork background (exact 3d tensor computation)
==============================================================================
  [PASS] 3d Ricci code == closed form R = e^{-2w}(-4 D^2 w - 2|Dw|^2)
  [PASS] R^(3) = -4 D^2 q + O(2); q = -lnN  =>  R^(3) = +4 D^2 Psi / c^2  -- R_lin = -4*Derivative(f(x1, x2, x3), (x1, 2)) - 4*Derivative(f(x1, x2, x3), (x2, 2)) - 4*Derivative(f(x1, x2, x3), (x3, 2))
  [PASS] gamma_ij pidot^ij = -2 D^2(q + lnN) + O(2)  == -2 * (flat) S2'  -- T_lin = -2*Derivative(f(x1, x2, x3), (x1, 2)) - 2*Derivative(f(x1, x2, x3), (x2, 2)) - 2*Derivative(f(x1, x2, x3), (x3, 2)) - 2*Derivative(nu(x1, x2, x3), (x1, 2)) - 2*Derivative(nu(x1, x2, x3), (x2, 2)) - 2*Derivative(nu(x1, x2, x3), (x3, 2))
  [PASS] on the fork surface q = -lnN:  r_3 = D^2(pdot) = -2 D^2[S2'] ~ 0 WEAKLY  -- r_3 vanishes as a multiple of the S2' constraint itself
  BASELINE CONTRAST (q = 0): gamma_ij pidot^ij = -2 D^2 lnN != 0 -- but in the
  baseline {pi_N, S2} = 0, so r_3 only fed the harmless mu_2.  In the fork the
  new E entry WOULD feed r_3 into mu_1 -- but r_3 is weakly zero.  So at
  Newtonian order:  mu_1 = -r_4 / L_N  with the FORK r_4.

  r_4 = -(Hperp_grav + sqrt(g) eps_n),  Hperp_grav(static) = -(c^4/16piG) sqrt(g) R
      = +(c^2/4piG) D^2 Psi - rho c^2        [R = 4 D^2 Psi/c^2 from above]
      = (c^2/4piG) [ D^2 Psi - 4piG rho ]
      = (c^2/4piG) D_i[(1-mu) D^i Psi]       [C_M = 0: D_i(mu D^i Psi) = 4piG rho]
  [PASS] D^2 Psi - D.(mu D Psi) == D.[(1-mu) D Psi]  (r_4 = phantom-density source)
  => r_4 = c^2 rho_ph  (rho_ph = MOND phantom density >= 0), NOT -rho c^2.
  BASELINE ANCHOR: q=0 gives R=0, r_4 = -rho c^2, chi eqn D.[c^2 M Dchi] = +4piG rho
  (attractive well) => the certified doubling g_m = g_N[1/mu + 1/M_par]. Same
  convention chain, fork r_4 sign FLIPS the chi channel.

