  [PASS] grad_mu T^{mu x}|_g = -rho dX/dx  (identity unchanged; MAGNITUDE is what moved)
  [PASS] Gauss: c^2 M_par chi' = -(1-mu) Psi' solves D.[c^2 M Dchi] = -D.[(1-mu) DPsi]
  Psi' > 0 (attractive well) => chi' < 0 => X = c^2 chi is a HILL: force OUTWARD.
  NET matter force (spherical):  g_matter = g_Psi [ 1 - (1-mu(y))/M_par(y) ],
  g_Psi = |D Psi| = y a0,  with the UNCHANGED exact AQUAL law mu(y) y a0 = g_N
  (C_M is untouched by the fork at Newtonian order: D_i corrections are O(Psi/c^2)).
  [PASS] net factor = (2 mu + y mu' - 1)/M_par  [mu_exp]
  [PASS] net factor = (2 mu + y mu' - 1)/M_par  [mu_5]
  [PASS] net factor = (2 mu + y mu' - 1)/M_par  [mu_10]

